WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.302
-Good evening.
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.770
This is "Late Night."
We hope you're doing well.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:05.472
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.472 --> 00:00:08.508
During the first ballot in
today's House speakership vote,

00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:10.042
Ohio congressman Jim Jordan

00:00:10.042 --> 00:00:14.280
fell short of the 217 votes
necessary to become speaker.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.716
But Republicans are determined
to keep trying

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.818
until they finally get it wrong.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.453
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:22.755
During the first ballot in
today's House speakership vote,

00:00:22.755 --> 00:00:24.090
several Republicans voted

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.993
for former New York
congressman Lee Zeldin,

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.894
which means they are
running out of options,

00:00:28.894 --> 00:00:30.964
even alphabetically.

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:31.931
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:33.600
"What about Ziggy Zyzax?

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:37.337
He's -- He's strong
on the border, right?"

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:39.005
Florida governor Ron DeSantis
over the weekend

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.906
announced that about
200 Floridians

00:00:40.906 --> 00:00:44.344
were evacuated from Israel
and landed in Tampa,

00:00:44.344 --> 00:00:46.546
marking the first time
in recorded history

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:49.249
that anyone was happy
to land in Tampa.

00:00:49.249 --> 00:00:50.516
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:52.652
"Well, maybe we'll
meet Tom Brady.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.854
What?

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.923
Retired?"

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.624
In a post today on Truth Social,

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:02.027
former president Trump said
that Ohio congressman Jim Jordan

00:01:02.027 --> 00:01:04.163
will be a great House speaker
and added that he had

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:06.532
his "complete and total
endorsement."

00:01:06.532 --> 00:01:09.035
"Good luck with that,"
said David Perdue, Kari Lake,

00:01:09.035 --> 00:01:11.704
Doug Mastriano,
Herschel Walker, Dr. Oz,

00:01:11.704 --> 00:01:14.440
and that kid he forced
to mow his lawn.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:16.909
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.377
It's a long list.

00:01:18.377 --> 00:01:22.448
Justice Amy Coney Barrett
said in an interview yesterday

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:25.285
that the Supreme Court
should adopt an ethics code

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:28.654
and added, "All nine justices
are very committed

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:31.390
to the highest standards
of ethical conduct."

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:34.460
And when he read that interview,
Clarence Thomas laughed so hard,

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:37.263
he almost fell off
a billionaire's yacht.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.131
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.131 --> 00:01:42.301
The drug manufacturer
Novo Nordisk announced yesterday

00:01:42.301 --> 00:01:45.204
that it has acquired
a new hypertension drug

00:01:45.204 --> 00:01:47.440
for $1.3 billion,

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:49.476
but they quickly
made that money back

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:52.011
after selling
five vials of insulin.

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:55.915
[ Audience groans ]

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:59.385
I guess my question is, where
did we think the laugh was?

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.553
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.553 --> 00:02:02.822
Like, as I'm saying it,
I'm like,

00:02:02.822 --> 00:02:04.724
"Wait, this might not work."

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:06.593
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.496 --> 00:02:12.131
Alright, well...

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:13.967
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:17.136
Got something pretty cool,
though,

00:02:17.136 --> 00:02:18.337
'cause you had to
suffer through that.

00:02:18.337 --> 00:02:20.506
Everybody look under your seat.
Vial of insulin.

00:02:20.506 --> 00:02:22.208
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:25.911
According to a new survey,

00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:28.948
baby boomers said
their top source for new slang

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:30.383
is younger family members.

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.385
Said your grandma,
"I crashed my whip

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.153
into the post office again."

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:37.123
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.558
According to the same survey,

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:41.794
the most popular new slang word
used in Florida is "sus."

00:02:41.794 --> 00:02:45.531
Well, yeah.
Have you ever been there?

00:02:45.531 --> 00:02:50.370
I'm surprised it's not also
the most popular baby name.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.705
"Yeah, we're calling him Sus.
We don't --

00:02:52.705 --> 00:02:54.674
Doesn't look like either of us."

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:57.309
[ Laughter ]

00:02:57.309 --> 00:03:00.380
Walmart has announced it will
offer the limited-edition

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:02.982
Van Leeuwen Kraft
Macaroni &amp; Cheese ice cream.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:06.352
It's a great way to make sure
your death is ruled a suicide.

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:08.954
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.954 --> 00:03:11.157
And finally --

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:13.559
You know would be good
with that?

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:16.562
Little vial of something.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:18.397
Not going to say what.

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:21.601
And finally, Coca-Cola
and the makers of Absolut Vodka

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.569
announced yesterday
they're planning to release

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:26.572
a new ready-to-drink
vodka-Sprite cocktail,

00:03:26.572 --> 00:03:29.041
because if you're mixing
vodka and Sprite,

00:03:29.041 --> 00:03:32.011
you're ready to drink.

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:35.915
Yeah, I don't know, just two
liquids, one of them alcohol.

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.316
And that was the monologue,
everybody.

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:38.418
We're off and running.

